  "wikitext": "{{Short description|Species of flowering plant}}\n{{speciesbox\n|image = Carlos Guilherme Rodrigues (76520007).jpeg\n|genus = Echium\n|species = tuberculatum\n|authority = Hoffm. & Link\n|}}\n\n'''''Echium tuberculatum''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] native to Portugal, Morocco, Algeria and Libya in the [[Iberian Peninsula]] and [[North Africa]] respectively.<ref>{{cite web |title=Echium tuberculatum Hoffmanns. & Link {{!}} COL |url=https://www.catalogueoflife.org/data/taxon/38MGH |publisher=[[Catalogue of Life]] |access-date=29 September 2021}}</ref> This plant is a hardy garden perennial and it forms a sprawling mass of red flowers during the whole of the summer.\n\nIt will self-seed readily.\n\n==References==\n{{reflist}}\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q5332615}}\n\n[[Category:Echium|tuberculatum]]\n[[Category:Flora of Portugal]]\n[[Category:Flora of North Africa]]\n\n\n{{Boraginoideae-stub}}",
